            "title": "JPMorgan's Dimon: Credit card cap would lead to 'economic disaster'",
            "description": "<p>One moment that stood out in JPMorgan Chase (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/JPM\">JPM</a>) CEO Jamie Dimon's interview at the World Economic Forum (WEF) in Davos, Switzerland, on Wednesday was when he referred to himself as <a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/news/jamie-dimon-declares-himself-a-globalist-in-davos-as-trump-barbs-linger-for-jpmorgan-145323782.html\">a \"globalist,\"</a> making light of President Trump's own comments calling the big bank executive \"a highly overrated globalist.</p>\n<p>Yahoo Finance Senior Bank Reporter <a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://www.yahoo.com/author/david-hollerith/\">David Hollerith</a> highlights the top takeaways from Dimon's remarks, sharing his thoughts on the Trump administration's policy proposals on credit card rate caps and the broader banking industry.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more\u00a0<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-domination/\">Market Domination</a>.</p>",
