            "id": "47ee8896-fd67-3877-bc84-b39e58764011",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "JPMorgan will likely have fewer employees in 5 years, CEO Dimon says",
            "description": "<p>At the World Economic Forum in Davos, Switzerland, JPMorgan Chase (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/JPM\">JPM</a>) CEO Jamie Dimon spoke about the impact AI will have on the global workforce and what companies and governments can do to help. Toward the end of the conversation, he was asked about jobs at JPMorgan Chase, and Dimon admitted that his \"guess\" is that the banking giant will have fewer employees in five years than it does today.</p>\n<p><a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://youtube.com/live/qc6LFeRe4xI\">Watch Dimon's full World Economic Forum discussion.</a></p>",
            "summary": "At the World Economic Forum in Davos, Switzerland, JPMorgan Chase (JPM) CEO Jamie Dimon spoke about the impact AI will have on the global workforce and what companies and governments can do to help. Toward the end of the conversation, he was asked about jobs at JPMorgan Chase, and Dimon admitted that his \"guess\" is that the banking giant will have fewer employees in five years than it does today. Watch Dimon's full World Economic Forum discussion.",
